linux-iprojection (1.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Added ESC/VP.net challenge-response authentication for passwords and 4-digit keywords.
  * Added modal keyword/password authentication dialog with persistent device store.
  * Added configurable casting resolutions (1080p, 720p, WXGA 1280x800, XGA 1024x768).
  * Socket buffer tuning (512KB) and MTU clamped to 1400 bytes to prevent Wi-Fi/VLAN drops.
  * Added multi-subnet Wake-on-LAN broadcast across ports 7 and 9 with direct MAC parsing.
  * Added EEMP dual-port discovery fallback to prevent bind conflicts.
  * Fixed unread stream buffering and thread-safe lazy lock event loop synchronization.

 -- John Varghese (J0X) <john@example.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

linux-iprojection (1.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bug fixes for log_writer TypeError on some PyGObject versions.
  * Added Adw.AlertDialog support.
  * Added enterprise-grade automated GitHub crash reporting.
  * GStreamer Caps negotiation fixed for VA-API (vah264enc) and NVENC.
  * Screen capture resolution dynamically bounded to 1080p for projector hardware limits.

 -- John Varghese (J0X) <john@example.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

linux-iprojection (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of iProjection (Unofficial) for Linux.
  * Native GTK4/Libadwaita user interface.
  * mDNS auto-discovery and PipeWire casting.
  * Direct ESC/VP advanced console and Wake-on-LAN support.

